        {
            "id": "F9B5C3FD-2091-49D6-9B3B-6BBDE0C3CEFD",
            "name": "Citizens Advice Sheffield",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "What does Citizens Advice do? Our Aims &amp; Principles\r\n\r\nCitizens Advice gives independent, impartial, free and confidential information and advice to help people overcome the problems they face, such as benefits, debt, employment, housing, relationships and immigration.\r\n\r\nWe use our knowledge about our clients&rsquo; problems to identify trends and campaign to improve the policies and practices that affect peoples&rsquo; lives.\r\n\r\nThe Citizens Advice service has 22,000 trained volunteers and 7,000 paid staff in 284 local Citizens Advice across England and Wales who provide an advice service to over 2.6 million people a year in over 2,500 locations in a range of ways including face to face, over the phone, by email and web-chat.\r\n\r\nWhat happens at Citizens Advice Sheffield?\r\n\r\nCitizens AdviceSheffield is part of the Citizens Advice network.\r\n\r\nWe are one of the country&rsquo;s largest Citizens Advice delivering advice and advocacy services to over 27,000 people a year. We deliver services by phone, digitally and face to face, from multiple locations, to some of Sheffield&rsquo;s most vulnerable communities.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://search.sheffieldvolunteercentre.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/https://citizensadvicesheffield.org.uk/about-us/volunteers-with-us/",
            "email": "volunteering@citizensadvicesheffield.org.uk",
            "phone": "01147006725",
            "website": "https://search.sheffieldvolunteercentre.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/https://citizensadvicesheffield.org.uk/about-us/volunteers-with-us/",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "PO Box 6222",
                    "latitude": 53.3989871,
                    "longitude": -1.4456138
                }
            ]
        },
