        {
            "id": "AE5CC599-5CBB-4A86-9D9A-3DA61528A4C7",
            "name": "Warrington BID",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Warrington BID covers the town centre and Stadium Quarter it is bounded by Mersey St, Wilson Pattern St Parker St and the Halliwell Jones Stadium.. It represents over 250 businesses spread across 300 commercial properties. We are a partnership between the businesses in the town centre. We work strategically with key organisations including Warrington and Co, Cheshire Police and Warrington Borough Council.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nOur BID members are diverse and include those from the private, public and voluntary sectors.\r\n\r\nSince being established in 2018, it has worked to a business agenda and delivered programme of works to help make the town centre a more attractive and safer place to visit. It organises and promotes events and markets the town centre as a shopping and leisure destination\r\n\r\nWe exist to help businesses in the town centre to sustainably grow and progress.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/WarringtonBID",
            "email": "Warringtonbid@groundwork.org.uk",
            "phone": "+447483932667",
            "website": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/WarringtonBID",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Warrington Town Centre",
                    "latitude": 53.390045166015625,
                    "longitude": -2.5969500541687012
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "4DC41658-435C-43CD-9F09-8B0B6F44C71E",
            "name": "St Joseph’s Hospice Hackney",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "What we do and who we care for\r\n\r\nFounded in 1905 by the Sisters of Charity, St Joseph&rsquo;s Hospice is one of the oldest and largest hospices in the UK. We provide, high quality, specialist palliative care and support to people in our local community who have a life-limiting illness. All our services are free of charge.\r\n\r\nOur core boroughs are Newham, City and Hackney, Tower Hamlets and&nbsp;City and Hackney, Tower Hamlets and&nbsp;, but some of our services are also available to people in the surrounding boroughs of Waltham Forest, Islington, Haringey and Enfield reaching a population of around 2.1 million people.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nWe take a holistic approach to our care, which means that we look after the wellbeing of the whole person, as well as their loved ones.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nWe provide palliative care in the Hospice and in the community as we believe that people should choose where they receive their care.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nOur range of services include:\r\n\r\n\r\n\tInpatient care\r\n\tPalliative care at home\r\n\tCommunity and day services\r\n\tTherapies\r\n\tCounselling and advice\r\n\t24 hour advice and support\r\n\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteers.newham.gov.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/StJoseph’sHospiceHackney",
            "email": "S.Bennett@STJH.org.uk",
            "phone": "020 8525 6000 ",
            "website": "https://volunteers.newham.gov.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/StJoseph’sHospiceHackney",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "St Joseph’s Hospice Hackney, Mare Street, Hackney ",
                    "latitude": 51.5370163,
                    "longitude": -0.056434500000000012
                }
            ]
        },
