        {
            "id": "2C355CEF-5250-4DAF-B4AB-356FE907E2F8",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "YHA Blaxhall makes a great base for exploring everything that the Suffolk coast has to offer. Comfortable and inviting, this former school is at the heart of the village, on the edge of Blaxhall Heath surrounded by wildlife and beautiful countryside.\r\n\r\nCurl up with a book in our cosy lounge, or relax on our garden picnic benches and enjoy being surrounded by flowers!\r\n\r\nThe hostel sits on the edge of the Suffolk Coast and Heaths Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty, one of the most important areas for wildlife in the whole of Britain. For bird watching, sea food, cycling and walking, YHA Blaxhall is a great options.\r\n\r\nJust down the road is the world famous Snape Maltings Concert Hall and you can walk around ancient burial mounds and discover the incredible&nbsp;story of the ship burial of an Anglo-Saxon King at Sutton Hoo.&nbsp; The magnificent 12th Century fortress of Framlingham Castle and the wild and remote shingle spit of Orford Ness are 8 and 6 miles away respectively.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThere is on-site parking.&nbsp; &nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHABlaxhall",
            "email": "blaxhallmanager@yha.org.uk",
            "phone": "01728 688206",
            "website": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHABlaxhall",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "The Old School House, Blaxhall, Woodbridge, Suffolk",
                    "latitude": 52.1606539,
                    "longitude": 1.46200239999996
                }
            ]
        },
