        {
            "id": "BAF06B91-252E-47FF-8762-48DDE9E906DA",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "YHA Streatley-on-Thames is a comfortable Victorian house five minutes&#39; walk from one of the prettiest stretches of the River Thames. At the crossroads of the Thames Path and Ridgeway National Trails, and with National Trust woodlands behind the youth hostel, there are plenty of leisurely walks and cycle rides in the vicinity that our staff can tell you about.\r\n\r\nWe are close to Reading and Oxford for some city attractions and there is a direct train link to London.\r\n\r\nVolunteering with YHA is a fantastic way to have fun, learn new skills, boost your CV and travel to different places. We have a variety of different opportunities to choose from and volunteering roles to suit everyone. &nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe tasks are varied and in return you will meet some great people, who both work and stay in our hostels, as well as enjoying your time off discovering the local area and attractions.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAStreatleyonthames",
            "email": "streatleymanager@yha.org.uk",
            "phone": "01491 872278",
            "website": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAStreatleyonthames",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Reading Road, Streatley, Berkshire",
                    "latitude": 51.50513,
                    "longitude": -1.10516
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "F283FF80-FD8F-4CB5-8C1E-69996449FAE3",
            "name": "Guide Dogs",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "We are Guide Dogs. And we&rsquo;re here to help people with sight loss live the life they choose.\r\n\r\nWe rely on our brilliant volunteers who give their time to help our charity in so many ways. There are many great volunteering opportunities to get involved in, even&nbsp;an hour makes a big difference.\r\n\r\nWe&nbsp;recognise the extraordinary efforts of all of our volunteers and&nbsp;we&#39;re&nbsp;really proud to have achieved the&nbsp;Investing in Volunteers&nbsp;accreditation for good practice in volunteer management.\r\n\r\nTogether, we can help people affected by sight loss live their lives to the full.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.communityactionderby.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/GuideDogs",
            "email": "volattractcentral@guidedogs.org.uk",
            "phone": "0345 143 0191",
