        {
            "id": "9C5F4783-3A0B-4BA2-BC0B-A30F675A4F05",
            "name": "University of East London",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe University of East London offers students interested in game development:\r\n\r\nYou&#39;ll learn from a mix of academics and industry professionals with experience in game design and development. Industry speakers provide insights on various topics, keeping you up-to-date with the latest trends. Throughout the course, you&#39;ll create games for simulated real-world briefs. This hands-on approach allows you to develop games for different demographics, marketplaces, and player types, developing games in a studio environment!\r\n\r\nMany UEL graduates have made their mark in the games industry. UEL offers three relevant programs, such as BA (Hons) Game Design, BSc (Hons) game programming and BA (Hons) 3D art for games which allow specialisation within the game design field- UEL equips you for a role in the expanding game industry.\r\n\r\nChoose UEL for a dynamic learning experience that bridges theory and practice, preparing you for an exciting career in game development!\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://vga.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/UniversityofEastLondon",
            "email": "iyounas@uel.ac.uk",
            "phone": "-",
            "website": "https://vga.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/UniversityofEastLondon",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "University of East London East Building",
                    "latitude": 51.5076668111111,
                    "longitude": 0.0643350888888889
                }
            ]
        },
