        {
            "id": "B925AEDD-1CB0-4743-A289-1056BA9E35B2",
            "name": "Sports Volunteering",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Sport Volunteering provides a wide range of opportunities for students and staff to volunteer in and around the local community. If you are looking for&nbsp;an opportunity to develop your skills, gain experience within sport and physical activity or&nbsp;to give back whilst having fun,&nbsp;we provide accessible sporting opportunities in multiple sports for&nbsp;all ages and abilities.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nCurrent popular junior opportunities volleyball, squash and tennis and childrens holiday sports camps.&nbsp;We also run a varied programme of&nbsp;sport and wellbeing opportunites for adults from hard to reach communities aimed at improving physical and mental health.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nStudents can also access our Community Sport Activator programme as part of their volunteering and receive mentoring and assistance in accessing formal qualifications, informal CPD as well as receiving a University recognised volunteering award.&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://durhamunivolunteering.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/teamdurhamcommunity",
