        {
            "id": "73628EC9-9118-41A1-B097-816017B6BA26",
            "name": "YHA Closed Hostels",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "This hostel is a rare Grade I listed Elizabethan manor house set in stunning National Trust countryside in the heart of Shropshire.&nbsp; With its Great Hall and spiral staircases it is a historic masterpiece and a quirky place to stay.&nbsp; It underwent a &pound;500,000 refurbishment in 2012 to bring it bang up to date. Perfect for people who enjoy walking as there is lovely countryside nearby and the waymarked trails of the Cardingmill Valley and the Long Mynd are just 7 miles away.&nbsp; Convenient for both the Ironbridge Gorge and its museums and the castle town of Ludlow.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe building is open to National Trust visitors between 2pm and 5pm on Wednesdays and Sundays.&nbsp; There are no locks on any of the bedroom doors&nbsp;owing to the age of the house.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nVolunteering with YHA is a fantastic way to have fun, learn new skills, boost your CV and travel to different places. We have a variety of different opportunities to choose from and volunteering roles to suit everyone. &nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe tasks are varied and in return you will meet some great people, who both work and stay in our hostels, as well as enjoying your time off discovering the local area and attractions.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAWilderhope",
            "email": "wilderhopemanor@yha.org.uk",
            "phone": "01694 771363",
            "website": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAWilderhope",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Longville in the Dale, Shropshire",
                    "latitude": 52.57803,
                    "longitude": -2.5815
                }
            ]
        },
