        {
            "id": "EB92FD43-B943-4F1D-854B-4C3DC06CDF45",
            "name": "Tees Valley Arts",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Tees Valley Arts is a charity that supports people to live creative lives. They have been working at the intersection of community and the arts for over 40 years. They are the only organisation committed to working across all five boroughs of the Tees Valley and across all art forms. Over the last 6 years they have developed a reputation for excellence in co-curating with communities leading to their recognition as an NPO in the most recent round of Arts Council funding. In recent years they have delivered co-curated programmes on behalf of TVCA, Middlesbrough Council, National Lottery Heritage Fund and Historic England. They are currently delivering the Redcar Palace project, establishing a new arts centre on the Redcar seafront on behalf of Redcar Council.&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nRedcar Palace is a home to;\r\n\r\n\r\n\tAn ongoing exciting exhibition programme featuring artists from our region and around the world\r\n\tHonestly Made Honestly Sold, our honesty shop featuring handmade and locally sourced goods from over 50 different local sellers\r\n\tBlooming Youth Collective &ndash; our peer led youth group for 16 to 24 year olds focused on wellbeing, inclusivity and friendship\r\n\tWhich Craft? Ladies, a free to attend drop-in craft group for women every Wednesdays\r\n\tLife drawing with Simon Edwards on Thursdays from 6pm to 8pm\r\n\tA community space to talk, learn and teach\r\n\r\n\r\nWe offer volunteer placements in a relaxed surroundings,&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\n\tWithin the gallery and outside the gallery&nbsp;\r\n\tFront of house\r\n\tWorking in a exhibition&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\tMedia\r\n\tPrinting\r\n\tCertain aspects of the business side&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://mvda.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/TeesValleyArts",
            "email": "dee@teesvalleyarts.org.uk",
            "phone": "07581155218",
            "website": "https://mvda.teamkinetic.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/TeesValleyArts",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Tees Valley Arts 28-29 Esplanade",
                    "latitude": 54.6189727783203,
                    "longitude": -1.06590247154236
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "A7BA282F-F838-4A6C-B511-45CEBA188B8F",
            "name": "The St John's Project (SJP)",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "The St John&rsquo;s Project (SJP) is a Registered Charity set up to provide support for St John the Baptist&rsquo;s church in Chester. This is the oldest building in the city still in use for its original purpose.&nbsp;It has a long and rich history intimately interwoven with that of Chester itself.\r\n\r\nThe SJP support takes two forms: managing a small cafe and shop and providing a guide service for visitors to the church. We need volunteers to help with both of these activities in a number of ways. The Church is open to visitors from 10 a.m. until 4p.m. Monday to Saturday (11 to 3 in winter). Sunday is for worship only.\r\n\r\nCafe and Shop\r\n\r\nThe cafe offers hot and cold drinks and packaged snacks at very reasonable prices from a purpose-built area within the church; while the shop provides a range of souvenirs and other articles.&nbsp; There are also hundreds of second-hand books and magazines for sale.\r\n\r\nGuide Service\r\n\r\nThere has been a church on this site since for almost 1400 years and the present church dates from 1075. So, there is an enormous fund of stories to tell.&nbsp; These have been condensed into a structured guided tour which is offered free to visitors.\r\n\r\nVolunteering Opportunities\r\n\r\nWe need enthusiastic people who can:\r\n\r\n\r\n\tAssist with the Cafe and Retail area;\r\n\tBe part of the Visitor experience in our Tour Service*;\r\n\tHelp with administration duties;\r\n\tDevelop and maintain our social media offerings;\r\n\tAssist&nbsp; with fund-raising; and\r\n\tGet involved in new schemes and projects.\r\n\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n*Full training will be provided\r\n\r\nFor an Application Form email:&nbsp;office@stjohnschester.uk\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteernowcwva.com/volunteers/provider-profile/TheStJohnsProjectSJP",
            "email": "murphya1948@gmail.com",
