                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "D2E6FC0F-3B73-4FA5-8B5C-06E44C14BF34",
            "name": "YHA Windermere",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Enjoy panoramic views of the lake and mountains from one of the most spectacularly situated YHA&#39;s in England. Overlooking England&rsquo;s largest natural lake, YHA Windermere offers the chance to stay in an idyllic countryside setting only 2 miles from Windermere and its many attractions and 4 miles from Ambleside.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nAn ideal base for anyone wanting to escape the crowds.&nbsp; The hostel has large wooded grounds with trails and wildlife to enjoy.&nbsp; &nbsp;Relax with a drink on the terrace and enjoy good quality food from the hostel&#39;s newly refurbished restaurant and bar.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nAround 100m from the hostel is a self-contained camping facility block and up to 20 campers can pitch there year round.&nbsp; Seasonally, bell tents and tipis are available.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nVolunteering with YHA is a fantastic way to have fun, learn new skills, boost your CV and travel to different places. We have a variety of different opportunities to choose from and volunteering roles to suit everyone. &nbsp;\r\n\r\nThe tasks are varied and in return you will meet some great people, who both work and stay in our hostels, as well as enjoying your time off discovering the local area and attractions.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAWindermere",
            "email": "windermeremanager@yha.org.uk",
            "phone": "015394 43543",
            "website": "https://volunteer.yha.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/YHAWindermere",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Bridge Lane, Troutbeck, Windermere, Cumbria",
                    "latitude": 54.37122,
                    "longitude": -2.91136
                }
            ]
        },
