        {
            "id": "426D0EE3-B164-4176-BA3D-B8B31691445F",
            "name": "KEEN London",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "KEEN London is a small but growing charity. Our vision is that every child has the chance to enjoy games and leisure activities and none are left behind due to disability.\r\n\r\n\r\nWe provide free games and activity sessions with tailored support for children with additional needs and disabilities. We support over 100 children, known as our &lsquo;athletes&rsquo;, with a wide range of additional needs, including autism, cerebral palsy, learning disabilities, and global development delay. At KEEN London, we strive to use fun and games to improve young people&#39;s wellbeing, personal, social and emotional development as well as broadening experiences to increase skills and confidence.\r\n\r\nFor more information, please visit:&nbsp;https://www.keenlondon.org/&nbsp;\r\n\r\nOr, you can keep up to date with KEEN London on Twitter, Facebook\r\n\r\nKEEN London is a registered charity, number&nbsp;1124915. It is also a limited company registered in England (number&nbsp;6579658), and its registered office is:\r\nUnit W1, 8 Woodberry Down,&nbsp;London, N4 2TG.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://barnetvolunteersc19.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/KEENLondon",
            "email": "volunteering@keenlondon.org",
            "phone": "07719 565307",
            "website": "https://barnetvolunteersc19.co.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/KEENLondon",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Unit 1",
                    "latitude": 51.572059631347656,
                    "longitude": -0.094013802707195282
                }
            ]
        },
