        {
            "id": "6AB463F8-C0BD-45F7-911F-01C090067CC2",
            "name": "Action in Mind (ST)",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Action in Mind is the leading local mental health charity predominantly working across the Stirling Council area, supporting better mental health for everyone.\r\n\r\nWe provide person-centred, outcome focused services for people from the age of 18 years experiencing low to moderate mental health conditions as well as people living with long-term chronic mental illnesses. We work closely with Stirling Council, NHS Forth Valley and Clackmannanshire and Stirling Health &amp; Social Care Partnership.\r\n\r\nAs partners to Stirling&rsquo;s Integrated Mental Health Service, four of our services form the mental health provision of Stirling&rsquo;s Integrated Mental Health Service and are provided for people 16 years and above, living in the Stirling Council area, who are experiencing or recovering from mental ill health &amp; related problems: -\r\n\r\nAdult Befriending - one-to-one befriending support provided by trained volunteers. This service is specifically for people who are socially isolated due to their mental illness, receive support from adult psychiatry and live in their own accommodation, and who are over 18 years of age.\r\n\r\nCounselling &ndash; person-centred counselling for people experiencing mild to moderate depression, anxiety or stress.\r\n\r\nThe Hub Centre &ndash; focuses on peer support and group activities such as health &amp; well-being, social activities, developing new skills, mental health self-management, etc.\r\n\r\nRural Outreach Service &ndash; supports people living in the rural areas of Stirling who are experiencing or recovering from mental ill health. The service aims to assist people to live a fulfilling life within their own community and endeavours to provide a service tailored to each person&rsquo;s needs.\r\n\r\nVolunteering underpins many of our services such as our volunteer befriending services or The Hub (peer support and group activities) with volunteers offering their enthusiastic support and commitment. All volunteers are vetted, trained and supported during their volunteering experience with us.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/volunteers/provider-profile/Action-in-Mind-(ST)",
            "email": "info@actioninmind.org.uk",
            "phone": "01786 451203",
            "website": "https://stirlingvolunteering.org/volunteers/provider-profile/Action-in-Mind-(ST)",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "19 Dean Crescent Riverside",
                    "latitude": 56.13075,
                    "longitude": -4.05001
                }
            ]
        },
