        {
            "id": "CDF9BDF7-A787-4BD4-BC91-3DCD120E2EC1",
            "name": "Park End (formerly Grow Well) Community Garden",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Grow Well is a Community Interest Company that aims to connect people through gardening.\r\n\r\nThe Grow Well Community Garden is within Vulcan&#39;s Park, Workington (Princess Street entrance).\r\n\r\nWe meet Thursday mornings, 10-12noon to spend time together gardening using organic, no-dig principles always mindful of wildlife. We grow flowering plants and vegetables and share any produce. We do have a non-activity time during the winter when we let the garden rest, as nature intends.\r\n\r\nAnyone is welcome to join us. Come with your ideas and questions. No gardening knowledge necessary. Some of our volunteers have a whole career&#39;s worth of gardening knowledge and skills to share with you. Or maybe you would just like to sit on our &#39;Settle&#39; and watch others garden.\r\n\r\nVulcan Park is within easy reach of both the bus and train station, being about 5-10mins walk from each.\r\n\r\nPlease be aware we have no toilets on site.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteering.cumbriacvs.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/GrowWellCommunityGarden",
            "email": "grow-well@hotmail.com",
            "phone": "07423657335",
            "website": "https://volunteering.cumbriacvs.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/GrowWellCommunityGarden",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Grow Well Community Garden/Vulcan Park",
                    "latitude": 54.640151977539062,
                    "longitude": -3.5529873371124268
                }
            ]
        },
