        {
            "id": "9E5D7071-DE05-412C-8963-1F323FA032A2",
            "name": "Warrington Youth Zone",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Our OnSide Youth Zone provides a provision for any Young Person aged 7-19 (up to 25 with additional needs). We offer a place to go, someone to talk to and something to do. We operate everyday of the year including bank holidays and weekends to offer the support any Young Person in and around Warrington. With over 20 Activites each night for our Juniors and our Seniors, we need an army of reliable and commited Volunteers. From Sports Volunteers to Admin Volunteers, we offer a wide range of oppitunities to accomidate most people. We must add on completion of training a Enhanced DBS will be required. For futher information please get in touch via volunteer@wyz.org.uk\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/WarringtonYouthZone",
            "email": "Aoife.Finlay@wyz.org.uk",
            "phone": "07360526127",
            "website": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/WarringtonYouthZone",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Warrington Youth Zone Dallam Lane",
                    "latitude": 53.392482757568359,
                    "longitude": -2.5958693027496338
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "14A9D488-7680-4583-9524-4E21A2965D45",
            "name": "SCC Tree Planting Team",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "Thank you for your interest in volunteering with Surrey&rsquo;s Tree Planting and Establishment Team. With your support we can work together to plant 1.2 million trees across Surrey to ease the effects of climate change and benefit biodiversity. We are hugely grateful that you have shown an interest in helping us.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\nVolunteers are at the heart of what we do and are essential to the running and continued success of our tree planting and establishment programme.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nWe are a small, friendly team delivering our tree planting objectives who are looking forward to seeing you this winter to help us plant trees!&nbsp;\r\n\r\nWhat to expect from your day\r\n\r\n\r\n\tWe offer morning and/or afternoon sessions, and sometimes for our larger sites you can stay all day if you wish.\r\n\tThere are scheduled tea and lunch breaks&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\tIt is essential that all volunteers wear suitable outdoor, comfortable clothing (layers are good and old clothing that you do not mind getting dirty in) and decent footwear such as walking boots or Wellingtons (no sandals, high heels or flip flops please - it has happened before!)&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\tWaterproof clothing is essential if it is a bit rainy and sunscreen/hats etc should be brought along for sunnier days&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\tPlease bring a packed lunch to enjoy a picnic alfresco together (under cover if it unfortunately rains), a foldable chair if you have one and a bottle of water too. ?&nbsp;\r\n\tYou will get all the details that you need for your volunteering session closer to the day.&nbsp; This includes directions, public transport links, parking, toilet facilites if there are any - or the nearest loos!\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy Spend the day with us\r\n\r\nBy tree planting with us you will get the opportunity to work outdoors in Surrey&rsquo;s beautiful countryside, and join an existing friendly volunteer tree planting team, offering a wide variety of benefits, including:&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\n\tFun, sociable and a great opportunity for healthy exercise&nbsp;\r\n\tGreat for mind, body and spirit as volunteering in the countryside has proven widespread health &amp; wellbeing benefits&nbsp;\r\n\tA great sense of personal achievement and self-worth&nbsp;\r\n\tAn opportunity to develop new skills and meet like-minded people&nbsp;\r\n\tImprove your employability by giving you valuable experience&nbsp;\r\n\tA safe, professionally led volunteering experience, as all our tasks are run by trained staff or Tree Wardens and are fully insured&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\nCorporate Volunteering\r\n\r\nWe also offer sessions for corporate groups.&nbsp; Please email trees@surreycc.gov.uk if you are interested in bringing your work team to volunteer.&nbsp; We can send you details of our rates for businesses.\r\n\r\nHow to get in Touch\r\n\r\nYou can email us at trees@surreycc.gov.uk\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://environmentvolunteering.surreycc.gov.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/VolunteerTreePlanting",
            "email": "trees@surreycc.gov.uk",
            "phone": "0300 200 1003",
            "website": "https://environmentvolunteering.surreycc.gov.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/VolunteerTreePlanting",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Surrey County Council 11 Woodhatch Road",
                    "latitude": 51.2263984680176,
                    "longitude": -0.200192004442215
                }
            ]
        },
