                    "address": "10 Leathermarket Court",
                    "latitude": 51.49838,
                    "longitude": -0.08949
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "5DECDC7B-1A05-4F86-802B-D6A99BD7AF49",
            "name": "Get Warrington Talking",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThrough local events, networking, campaigns and conversations we will create a culture of knowledge and understanding around mental health, mental illness and suicide prevention.\r\n\r\nWe will strengthen the support networks within the town for people experiencing mental health challenges and endeavour to ensure that everyone can access the help they need when they need it.\r\n\r\nIf you live or work in Warrington and you have a lived mental health experience, then we want to hear from you. We are keen to grow the number of Get Warrington Talking champions so that we can positively engage with our local communities, challenging stigma and discrimination.\r\n\r\nWe are always looking to involve new champions in our activities, for more information please contact GWT@warringtonspeakup.org.uk or call 01925 246938 or visit our&nbsp;Facebook&nbsp;/&nbsp;Twitter&nbsp;/&nbsp;Instagram&nbsp;page.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/GetWarringtonTalking",
            "email": "GWT@warringtonspeakup.org.uk",
            "phone": "01925 246938",
            "website": "https://volunteering.warringtonva.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/GetWarringtonTalking",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "89 Sankey Street",
                    "latitude": 53.3885348,
                    "longitude": -2.5986829
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "03A6CFD3-0E19-405B-BACD-76160D02452F",
            "name": "Cheshire Wildlife Trust",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "As a volunteer at Cheshire Wildlife Trust you&rsquo;ll be joining a network of over 350 like-minded people, who give anything from a few hours to a few days each year to support our work across Cheshire.&nbsp;\r\nWe have a wide range of volunteering opportunities to get involved with. Everything from getting your hands dirty on a nature reserve, to supporting at events and open days or helping with office admin.\r\n\r\nVery simply, we couldn&rsquo;t do what we do without volunteers. You don&rsquo;t always need to be an expert to get involved, full training and support is given for all our activities. You&rsquo;ll have the chance to meet new people, learn new skills and share your experience with others. Being a volunteer with us is a rewarding experience, that&#39;s why our volunteers keep coming back.\r\n\r\nPlease note, unless it is specified on the volunteer opportunity we are unable to accept volunteers under the age of 18.\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteering.cvsce.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/CheshireWildlifeTrust",
            "email": "astubbs@cheshirewt.org.uk",
            "phone": "07519326122",
            "website": "https://volunteering.cvsce.org.uk/volunteers/provider-profile/CheshireWildlifeTrust",
            "location": [
                {
                    "address": "Bickley Farm Bickley Wood",
                    "latitude": 53.025299072265625,
                    "longitude": -2.7186059951782227
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "53540D01-451A-4EBE-8347-FC51DDFA6EA5",
            "name": "Green Island Holiday Trust",
            "type": "Organisation",
            "description": "We are a Dorset based charity providing supported holidays for local people living with a disability.&nbsp;Every summer we create a touch of holiday magic by bringing together small groups of holidaymakers with teams of dedicated volunteers for a week of friendship and fun.\r\n\r\nOur holidays are based at Wraxall Yard, situated in the peaceful hamlet of Lower Wraxall, near Dorchester. Surrounded by beautiful countryside, Wraxall Yard is a beautifully transformed set of previously derelict barns, adapted to the highest of standards to provide accessible accommodation for people living with disabilities.&nbsp;The site is at the centre of an organic family farm and also features a livestock barn and workshop for visitors to get involved in farming and wildlife activities.\r\n\r\nhttps://greenislandholidaytrust.com\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n",
            "applylink": "https://volunteer.can100.org/volunteers/provider-profile/Green-Island-Holiday-Trust",
            "email": "philippa@greenislandholidaytrust.com",
            "phone": "01202 375006",
